---
title: Beef Stifado
cooklang: 2
servings: 6
cuisine: Greek
source: recipe-pack dinner-3/4535-beef-stifado-2
---

= Marinade -> marinated beef

`Place` @stewing beef{1.5%kg}(trimmed, cut into 7 cm pieces) in a large #bowl{} and `add`
@garlic{3%cloves}(peeled, finely sliced), @bay leaves{3}, @allspice berries{1.5%tsp}, @cloves{6},
@cinnamon stick{1}, @dried oregano{1%tsp}, @red wine{125%ml} and @red wine vinegar{4%tbsp}.

`Cover` and `marinate` in the #fridge{} for ~chill{6%hours}.

= Stew -> stifado

`Peel` @baby onions{24} on a #board{} and `chop` @tomatoes{4}(ripe) roughly.

`Heat medium` @olive oil{4%tbsp} in a large #saucepan{} over medium heat and `sauté` the @&baby onions{}
in the #&saucepan{} for ~{5%minutes} until ~{softened}. `Remove` the @&baby onions{} with a
#slotted spoon{} to a #plate{}.

`Brown` the @&stewing beef{} from the marinade in the #&saucepan{} for
~{8-10%minutes} on all sides.

`Return` the @&baby onions{} to the #&saucepan{}, `add` the @&marinated beef{}, the @&tomatoes{},
@tomato purée{1%tbsp} and @-water{500%ml} to the #&saucepan{}, to just cover.

`Season` with @sea salt{} and @black pepper{}. `Bring` to the boil, then `simmer` for
~{90-120%minutes} until ~{the beef is tender and the sauce has thickened}.

`Serve` with @?pasta{} and @?hard cheese{}(grated).
